# Symmetry-mode analysis (crystod-group --supergroup-cif); testsuite section 23
# AMPLIMODES-style decomposition of a group-subgroup distortion into parent irreps
# with mode amplitudes, checked against Bilbao AMPLIMODES (D. Orobengoa et al.,
# J. Appl. Cryst. 42, 820 (2009)): SrTiO3 Pm-3m -> I4/mcm R5- 0.3303 A and
# ZrO2 Fm-3m -> P4_2/nmc X2- 0.5773 A are the first two runs below.
#
# Run the commands inside this directory; every output is written here. The
# ScF3 run reads its parent from ../test_POSCARs/221_PPOSCAR_ScF3.
#
# Every run also writes one VESTA file per activated irrep,
# {supergroup_file}_{irrep}.vesta, showing that irrep's displacement pattern as
# arrows on the parent-derived reference structure (invariant-core cell; the
# largest arrow is scaled to 1.5 A). The CaTiO3 Pm-3m -> Pnma pair, for example,
# writes 221_PPOSCAR_CaTiO3_{X5+,M2+,M3+,R4+,R5+}.vesta (X5+ 0.5196, M2+ 0.0064,
# M3+ 0.8874, R4+ 1.2458, R5+ 0.1047 A; total 1.6188 A):
#   crystod-group --supergroup-cif 221_PPOSCAR_CaTiO3.cif --subgroup-cif 62_PPOSCAR_CaTiO3.cif

# Non-special (symmetry line) k points are supported: the Pbam
# antiferroelectric of PbZrO3 (8x the cubic cell) condenses SM = (1/4,1/4,0)
# and S = (1/4,1/2,1/4) order parameters on top of R/X/M ones; all AMPLIMODES
# amplitudes are reproduced (SM2 1.2871, R4+ 1.5232, S4 0.4470, R5+ 0.0810,
# X3- 0.0374, M5- 0.0473 A). debug2_PbZrO3/ is not in the pip package (it stays
# in the CrystOD development tree).
#   crystod-group --supergroup-cif debug2_PbZrO3/POSCAR_PbZrO3_Pm-3m.cif --subgroup-cif debug2_PbZrO3/POSCAR_PbZrO3_Pbam.cif
#
# A second line-point case, the K2SeO4 lock-in ferroelectric (Pnma -> Pna2_1,
# 3x along a, SM = (1/3,0,0); the amplitudes of the AMPLIMODES analysis --
# GM1+ 0.9467, GM4- 0.4230, SM2 1.2885, SM3 0.1727 A, total 1.6629 A):
#   crystod-group --supergroup-cif POSCAR_K2SeO4_Pnma.cif --subgroup-cif POSCAR_K2SeO4_Pna21.cif
#
# Every run also saves the transformation matrix (parent -> child, AMPLIMODES
# convention) and the decomposition table as sym_mode_{formula}
# (sym_mode_K2SeO4, ...), named by the parent composition; --output-dir DIR
# writes the table and the VESTA files into DIR instead. Use it when two parents
# have the same composition. POSCAR_La3Ni2O7_I4mmm.cif -> POSCAR_La3Ni2O7_Cmcm.cif
# is the La3Ni2O7 pair of the last run below, with the child in an equivalent
# description (GM1+ 0.1313 A, X3- 1.1414 A against 1.1413 A there, total
# 1.1489 A); --output-dir keeps its sym_mode_La3Ni2O7 apart from that run's:
#   crystod-group --supergroup-cif POSCAR_La3Ni2O7_I4mmm.cif --subgroup-cif POSCAR_La3Ni2O7_Cmcm.cif --output-dir La3Ni2O7_I4mmm_Cmcm
#
# The direction column follows ISOTROPY: each order parameter is named by the
# ISOTROPY representative of its stratum, the row that
# "crystod-group --parent SG --irrep IR" lists (section 17), whichever
# domain-equivalent orientation the child file describes. When the child as
# given sits on another direction of the stratum, a "(direction: ...)" note
# under the table names it: the SrTiO3 run prints R5- (0,0,a), the I4/mcm row
# of --parent Pm-3m --irrep R5-, and notes R5- (a,0,0); V2O3 R-3c -> C2/c
# (debug9_V2O3/, not in the pip package) prints GM3+ (a,0) and notes
# GM3+ (0.577a,-a). With several irreps the largest mode sits on its --parent
# row and the others on the directions of the same domain (ScF3 Pbnm:
# R4+ (0,a,a) with M3+ (a;0;0)). The cell relation, the displacements, the
# amplitudes and the VESTA files follow the input files.
#
# Further inputs of testsuite section 23:
#   POSCAR_FeS2_Pa-3 / POSCAR_FeS2_P1_fcc2 -- pyrite-type FeS2 with seeded random
#     displacements (0.03 A rms) in the fcc-type double cell: complex-type irreps
#     are listed as one line per conjugate pair (R1+R3+, GM2+GM3+), pseudoreal
#     ones (R2+, R2-) keep one name; total 0.2540 A:
#     crystod-group --supergroup-cif POSCAR_FeS2_Pa-3 --subgroup-cif POSCAR_FeS2_P1_fcc2
#   POSCAR_KGeCl3_P4mmm_pseudo / POSCAR_KGeCl3_Cm -- KGeCl3 (Materials Project
#     mp-998231) against a P4/mmm pseudo-parent: the least-distortion mapping is a
#     twin setting, so the mapping is redone in a group-subgroup setting (NOTE
#     line); GM3- 0.1702 A, GM5- 0.2482 A:
#     crystod-group --supergroup-cif POSCAR_KGeCl3_P4mmm_pseudo --subgroup-cif POSCAR_KGeCl3_Cm
#   POSCAR_SeO2_Cmme_pseudo / POSCAR_SeO2_Pmc21 -- SeO2 (mp-560882) against a
#     Cmme pseudo-parent: no group-subgroup mapping exists (Wyckoff conflict, a
#     parent mirror fixes 8 O sites of the reference but 4 O atoms of the child);
#     the run stops with that message (exit status 1):
#     crystod-group --supergroup-cif POSCAR_SeO2_Cmme_pseudo --subgroup-cif POSCAR_SeO2_Pmc21
#   POSCAR_GaN2_P6mmm / POSCAR_GaN2_P21 -- a synthetic hexagonal line-star case
#     (P6/mmm, Ga on 1a, N on 2d; the Ga atoms of a cell four times longer along c
#     displaced in the plane): a single DT6 mode at (0,0,1/4) gives P2_1, 0.0949 A:
#     crystod-group --supergroup-cif POSCAR_GaN2_P6mmm --subgroup-cif POSCAR_GaN2_P21
# Structures from the Materials Project (mp-998231 KGeCl3, mp-560882 SeO2), CC BY 4.0;
# A. Jain et al., APL Mater. 1, 011002 (2013). The *_pseudo files are modified
# (group-averaged pseudo-parent) structures.

